# Backend Rules

## Thin controllers

```php
// Controller: HTTP only
public function authenticate(LoginRequest $request) {
    $request->authenticate();
    $request->session()->regenerate();
    return $this->redirectForRole(Auth::user());
}
```

Move validation, rate limits, and external API calls to Form Requests or Services.

## File organization

| Concern | Path |
|---------|------|
| Controllers | `app/Http/Controllers/` |
| Validation | `app/Http/Requests/` |
| Middleware | `app/Http/Middleware/` |
| Business logic | `app/Services/` or `app/Actions/` |
| Models | `app/Models/` |
| Routes | `routes/web.php`, `routes/api.php` |

## Routes

- Named routes with dot prefix: `fleet.dashboard`, `admin.dashboard`.
- Group by `prefix`, `middleware`, and `name()`.
- Replace fat closures in `web.php` with controller methods as features grow.

## Do not

- Skip Form Requests for validated endpoints.
- Hardcode roles in many places — use middleware/policies.
- Return sensitive fields in JSON without API Resources.
